# Work content

## Frontmatter

- `description` — project statement (one or more paragraphs, blank-line separated); left column beside media
- `seoDescription` — short meta / Open Graph blurb (≤160 chars); do not paste the essay into meta
- `year` — use a hyphen for ranges; ongoing projects are `2020-Ongoing`
- `video.loop: true` — UI shows “Loop”; do not show a duration for loops
- `order` — controls Works index sort (higher / configured order as used on `/works`)

## Cross-work links

In `description`, link other works with markdown: `[Pinchard’s Island](/pinchards-island)`. Rendered as body-coloured text with a faint grey underline. Do not self-link the current work’s title.

## Prose punctuation

Do not use em dashes (—) or en dashes (–) in `description` or `seoDescription`. Prefer commas, periods, colons, or parentheses. Hyphens only in compound words and year ranges (`2020-Ongoing`).

## Titles + slugs

- Keep **Light House** / `light-house` (two words). Do not rename to Lighthouse — the split is intentional (lighted house vs maritime lighthouse).

## Gallery JSON captions

Structured fields on each image, rendered as one line joined by ` • ` (empty fields skipped):

`title` · `date` · `dimensions` · `notes` · optional freeform `caption`

```json
{
  "src": "https://media.adamsimms.xyz/work/cabin/01.avif",
  "fallback": "https://media.adamsimms.xyz/work/cabin/01.jpg",
  "alt": "Cabin interior",
  "title": "Interior, daylight",
  "date": "2018",
  "dimensions": "24 × 36 in",
  "notes": "Archival pigment print"
}
```

Prefer AVIF + JPG `fallback`. Prefer specific `alt` text; generic title-only alts become `"{title}, image N of M"` in the gallery.

## Video + stills

For video-primary works where stills should not share the hero carousel, set `stillsAfterBody: true`. Hero shows video only; gallery images render as a **Reference** thumbnail grid below the essay and open in a lightbox.

## Documentation stills (non-video)

Optional `documentation` array in the gallery JSON (same image shape as `images`). Shown below the essay as the **Documentation** grid when `stillsAfterBody` is not used — e.g. process photos while the hero keeps the work gallery.


## Hidden works

These stay live at their URLs but are excluded from the sitemap and get `noindex, nofollow`:

`from-to`, `washed-up`, `newfoundland`

Source of truth: `HIDDEN_WORK_SLUGS` / `HIDDEN_PATHS` in `src/lib/seo.ts` (imported by `astro.config.mjs` for the sitemap filter). Mirror the page-level `noindex` flag when adding or removing a hidden work.
